---
title: Cold Brew Concentrate
description: Toddy cold brew concentrate from a full pound of coffee, steeped for a day at room temperature.
tags: [coffee, make-ahead]
course: drink
icons: [coffee-beans, jug, jar]
difficulty: easy
source:
  name: Toddy
  url: https://toddycafe.com/downloads/toddy_retail_instructions.pdf
adapted: true
time: 24h10m
---

> **Grind** — Grind the coffee on the coarsest setting, or ask the shop for a French press grind.

Push the #stopper{} into the outside bottom of the #Toddy brewing container{}. Dampen the #felt filter{} and press it into the inside bottom.

Pour a cup of @filtered water{1%cup} into the container, then add half the @coarse-ground coffee{8%oz}.

Slowly pour half the remaining @&filtered water{4%cup} over the grounds in a circular motion. Wait ~bloom{5%minutes}.

Add the rest of the @&coarse-ground coffee{8%oz}, then slowly pour in the rest of the @&filtered water{4%cup}. It will fill the container nearly to the brim. Lightly press the top of the grounds with the back of a #spoon{} until they're all wet. Don't stir. Stirring can clog the felt filter.

Steep at room temperature for ~steep{24%hours}.

Set the container on the #glass decanter{} and pull the stopper. Let the concentrate drain through.

> **If It Won't Drain** — Poke the blunt end of a dinner knife down through the grounds until it touches the filter, then gently scrape the top of the filter.

> **Storing** — Keeps in the decanter, lidded, in the refrigerator for up to 2 weeks.

To serve, start with 1 part concentrate to 2 parts water or milk, then add more to taste. A full pound brews stronger than Toddy's standard 12 oz batch, so expect to go past 1 to 2. Pour over ice for iced coffee, or stir into steaming hot water for hot.

> **Cleaning the Filter** — Rinse the felt filter with water and no soap, then freeze it damp in a resealable bag. One filter lasts 10 batches or 3 months.

> **What's Changed** — The coffee, water and method are Toddy's. Toddy only gives the layer sizes for a 12 oz batch, so the split of the 9 cups here is scaled up from that.
